                <pb facs="0634" n="510" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg510"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102 Ic/5: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Charge in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Ruddock</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-07-06T18:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 6, 1921—6
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received July 6—6:03 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>248. My 247, July 5, 5 p.m. Consulate general at Hankow reports large mass
                    meeting Chinese at Ichang resulting in resolutions for international settlement
                    along lines of Chefoo including international volunteer corps and international
                    municipal council. Resolutions signed by President of Chinese Chamber of
                    Commerce, et cetera. It emphasizes plan will not be detrimental to sovereignty
                    of China.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ruddock</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
